  "description": "The Reid eTrail 1.5 is engineered to deliver an exhilarating off-road riding experience without breaking the bank. With its durable construction and reliable components, this electric bike is designed to handle the demands of trail riding while offering excellent value for money.\nThe eTrail 1.5 features a sturdy alloy frame with integrated battery and mid mounted motor, providing a stable platform for tackling rough terrain. Its rigid design ensures responsive handling and precise control, allowing you to navigate technical trails with confidence.\nEquipped with a 100mm travel Suntour through axle suspension fork, the eTrail 1.5 absorbs bumps and impacts to provide a smoother ride over uneven surfaces. Whether you're climbing steep hills or descending rocky trails, the suspension fork helps maintain traction and stability for maximum control.\nThe eTrail 1.5 comes equipped with a range of reliable components to enhance performance and durability. From the Shimano 9-speed drivetrain for smooth shifting to the Shimano hydraulic disc brakes for reliable stopping power, every aspect of this bike is designed to deliver a dependable ride.\nWith a 36V 250W 80NM motor, the eTrail 1.5 offers ample power to assist you on climbs and accelerate quickly on flats. Whether you're commuting to work or exploring off-road trails, the motor provides the extra boost you need to tackle hills and cover more ground with ease.\nThe eTrail 1.5 is powered by a 36V/11.6Ah battery, providing enough juice for long rides without frequent recharges. With a capacity of 418Wh, this battery offers a respectable range, allowing you to explore further and ride for extended periods without worrying about running out of power.\nWhether you're a seasoned trail rider or a novice explorer, the Reid eTrail 1.5 is your ticket to adventure. With its durable construction, reliable mid motor performance, and affordable price tag, this electric trail bike is ready to take you on unforgettable off-road journeys.\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike and eScooter safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
